---
fmContentType: glossaryEntry
term: "Phenotype"
letter: "P"
anchor: "phenotype"
category: "growing"
---

The physical expression of a plant's genetics — how a particular plant actually grows, looks, smells, and produces cannabinoids and terpenes. Two seeds from the same strain can produce plants (phenotypes) with noticeably different characteristics. This is why experienced growers "pheno-hunt" — growing multiple plants from the same genetics to find the individual that best expresses the desired traits.
